    "text": "Let p ⩾ 673 be a prime and r ⩾ 2 be an integer. Let B be the free group\nin the Burnside variety of exponent p on a1 , . . . , ar . Must every non-identical one-\nvariable equation w(a1 , . . . , ar , x) = 1 over B have at most finitely many solutions\nin B?                                                                        A. Gaglione",
